# Basic 3-way handshake with all the options we negotiate.
#
# Verifies:
#  - SYN carries SYN+ECE+CWR flags (ECN-Setup, RFC 3168)
#  - SYN options: MSS=1460, wscale=5, sackOK, TS val ecr 0
#  - SYN-ACK from peer with ECE confirms ECN
#  - Our third ACK echoes peer's TSval

--connect 10.0.0.1:49152 10.0.0.2:80

# Our SYN: ECN-Setup flags + full option set, seq=0 (relative), ack=0.
# TS val captured as $cli_ts for later echo verification.
+0 > SEW 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460, wscale 5, sackOK, TS val $cli_ts ecr 0>

# Peer's SYN-ACK 5ms later: confirms ECN (ECE without CWR), echoes our
# TSval, advertises its own window scale and sackOK.
+.005 < SE. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 32768 <mss 1460, wscale 7, sackOK, TS val 1000 ecr $cli_ts>

# Our third ACK: pure ACK, echoes peer's TSval=1000, ECT(0) marked at IP
# layer (ECN is now negotiated and SYN-ACK was confirming).
+0 > . 1:1(0) ack 1 ecn ECT0 <nop,nop,TS val * ecr 1000>

--expect_state ESTABLISHED
